      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We begin by noting that since the radius and semi-major axis are perpendicular to each other, they will create a right triangle. We start by calculating the distance between the foci for the ellipse with semi-major axis 5 and semi-minor axis 4. Note that the difference between the side lengths of a central-angle triangle is the distance between the foci, so we have$$ (5^2 - 4^2)^{1/2} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{41}},$$ meaning the remaining distance is a radius of the circle. We then conclude that the radius of the circle is $\\sqrt{41}-4$.",
