      "text": "[asy]import olympiad;\nsize(200);\nreal f = 5 - sqrt(3);\ndraw(scale(f)*unitcircle);\npath major = (f,0)..(0,f)..(-f,0);\npath minor = (0,0)--(0,f)--(1.3333,2.6666)--(-1.3333,2.6666)--cycle;\ndraw(major);\ndraw(minor);\ndraw(Circle((f,0),f));\ndraw(Circle((0,f),f));\ndraw(Circle((-f,0),f));\ndraw(Circle((0,-f),f));\npair A = (3,0), B = (0,4);\ndraw(B--A--(f,0)--cycle);\ndot((1.97,0.88)); dot((0,4.12));\nlabel(\"A\",A,S); label(\"B\",B,N);\nlabel(\"$f$\",f*(1,0),S);\nlabel(\"$a$\",0,2*f/W);\nlabel(\"$b$\",1.3333*2*f/N,2*f);\nlabel(\"$c$\",f*2/N,2*f);[/asy]\nLet's write a Python program.\nimport math\n\n# Major axis length\na = 5\n\n# Minor axis length\nb = 4\n\n# Using one focus as a center, a circle is drawn that is tangent to the ellipse,\n# no part of the circle is outside the ellipse\n\n# a^2 = b^2 + c^2\n# c = a^2 - b^2\nc = a**2 - b**2\n\n# then we can find 4 different value:\n# - a, c, size of circle are 1st instance of the ellipse\n# - a, b, size of circle are 2nd instance of the ellipse\n# - b, c, size of circle are 3r instance of the ellipse\n# - a+b+c, c, size of circle is fourth instance of the ellipse\n# In this case, we want 4th instance, so we set:\nr = (a+b+c)/2\nprint(r)",
